# Testing Standards

## Framework
- **Server**: Mocha + Chai + Sinon (`cd server && npm test`)
- **Client**: `ng e2e` configured; no `*.spec.ts` unit tests exist yet — TODO: confirm with team

## File Location & Naming
- MUST place server tests under `server/test/<domain>/`
- MUST name files `<subject>.test.js` (e.g. `jwtLifecycleSecurity.test.js`)
- Security tests MUST live in `server/test/authorization/`

## Structure (AAA)
```js
describe('Security - feature name', () => {
  before(async () => { /* setup express app + runtime mocks */ });
  after(async () => { /* close server */ });

  it('MUST return 403 when user lacks admin group', async () => {
    // Arrange: create token with limited groups
    // Act:     const res = await request(server, { path, headers });
    // Assert:  expect(res.statusCode).to.equal(403);
  });
});
```

## Mocking Policy
- MUST use real Express HTTP requests via `http.request` (see existing tests)
- MAY stub external devices/protocols with Sinon; MUST NOT mock away auth checks under test
- MUST use test-only secrets (e.g. `const SECRET = 'jwt-lifecycle-secret'`), never production values

## Coverage Expectations
- MUST add tests for: new/changed auth paths, input validation, path normalization, rate limiting
- MUST add tests for: new device datatype parsing or storage insert/select logic
- SHOULD add tests for: bug fixes that reproduce a reported failure
- TODO: confirm with team — no enforced coverage threshold in CI

## What Does NOT Need Tests
- Pure UI styling/CSS changes
- MkDocs-only documentation edits
- Generated or vendored assets in `client/src/assets/lib/`
